From 6b6254a7e59eebb6736abb29fb816b8552cc9e14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:56:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] session outcome judge binds the chat's owning
 profile scope when its caller bound none

Notice writers (kanban_unloaded / kanban_remote_notices), orphan reap, completion notes and the web
refresh call refresh_outcome[s_quietly] from sweeper threads or handlers whose context has no profile
secret scope. On the multiplexed hub gateway the session-outcome judge's provider read then failed at
0.0 s with UnscopedSecretError (ANTHROPIC_TOKEN), e.g. agent.log 2026-11-12 16:23:34 right before
'kanban sweep wake ... busy, notice row written', and 17:00:44/51. cff30b6592 only scoped the post-turn
refresh.

_judge_summary now runs the judge inside _owner_scope(db): under multiplexing with no secret scope
bound, it binds the owner of <home>/state.db (home override + owner_secret_scope(home), as routed turns
do) and restores the caller's context after. A caller that already bound a scope keeps it; a
single-profile process binds nothing.

Proof: tests/hermes_state/test_outcome_judge_owner_scope.py is RED on origin/main (5 failed, the
refresh/derive cases with the production UnscopedSecretError) and GREEN with the fix (7 passed). The
19 test files importing hermes_state_outcome + test_split_module_imports: 410 passed. Each of the three
guard conditions mutated away fails one test. Task t_01a1d0d08799272e.
